cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it. The current work is PSAO, in
  psao-artifact/. Material under results/, load-tests/ and the root manifests
  belongs to the earlier study and is retained for provenance.
title: "PSAO: predictive security-aware offloading of JWT verification in a Zero Trust service mesh"
abstract: >-
  A Kubernetes testbed and reproducibility artifact for measuring event-loop
  saturation in a Node.js microservice under layered Zero Trust enforcement
  (Edge TLS, Istio mTLS, application-level JWT validation with HS256 and RS256),
  modelling the service as a single-server queue, and evaluating PSAO -- a
  controller that relocates token verification into the Envoy sidecar before the
  saturation point is reached and reverts, with hysteresis, when load falls back.
  Includes open-loop load generation, a four-stage decomposition of jwt.verify(),
  and the analysis pipeline that produces the paper's figures and LaTeX macros.
